{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi James, sorry things are slow today. I checked your desktop and found nothing obviously wrong. It has plenty of free disk space and no warnings. A few quick questions so I can narrow this down: 1) Are you in the office today or working from home on VPN? 2) Is it only the shared drives that are slow, or are websites, Teams and email slow too? 3) Is one particular shared folder slow, or all of them? 4) Are coworkers near you seeing the same slowness? 5) Which computer are you on right now? Your office desktop isn't showing as connected on our side. While you're checking, here are some things to try: if you're on VPN, disconnect and reconnect it. Shared drives are always slower over VPN, so large files open faster from OneDrive or SharePoint. Pause any big uploads or downloads, like OneDrive sync or backups. Use a wired connection or move closer to the Wi-Fi if you can. And if the computer hasn't been fully restarted in a few days, restart it (a real restart, not just sleep). Let me know what you find and whether any of these help.",
  "internal_note": "P3 slow file shares / general slowness. lookup_user: James O'Connor, Ops Warehouse Supervisor, account active and healthy, one device BL-DT-0108 (desktop). check_device_status BL-DT-0108: OFFLINE, last check-in 2026-10-09 12:21 UTC, 400 GB free (78%), no warnings, so low disk is ruled out. Sign-in logs: normal, all Chicago, MFA OK. He alternates between corporate network (m365 from 203.0.113.10) and home VPN (residential 198.51.100.28). No security concerns. It's unclear whether he's in the office or on VPN today, and the desktop being offline doesn't fit with him actively using it. He may be on another machine. Sent KB-015/KB-019 self-help steps (VPN reconnect, pause sync, wired/Wi-Fi, restart) and asked for scope. Per KB-015, escalate to Tier 2/network if he confirms the whole office is slow or one share is slow for everyone. Per KB-019, escalate if he's still slow after restart/updates. No actions queued.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-015",
    "KB-019"
  ],
  "confidence": "medium"
}
